  "notes": "v239 — NAV-MAP-COLORS-3D (owner, Fri Oct 23, 2026 11:36 MDT: the colours on our map are abysmal — pale beige/washed against the Rand McNally benchmark of saturated greens/blues and clear roads). RE-BASELINE ON THE FIXED BUILD first: with the v235 z15 tiles painting real content, what remained washed was Esri World Street Map palette itself. Measured on the LIVE tiles (z15, the level the drive layer fetches): Esri WSM mean saturation 0.150 on his home tile / 0.126 downtown; OSM standard on the same tiles measures LOWER (0.103 / 0.106); Esri World Topo is near-greyscale at z15 here (0.000 / 0.011); CARTO still demands an API key. So NO source swap beats the shipped source — the fix is a MEASURED colour lift on the same proven tiles, scoped to the drive street layer only via a new nv-tile-street class: contrast(1.06) saturate(1.38). Simulated on the live tiles before shipping: home saturation 0.150 -> 0.202 (+35%), downtown 0.126 -> 0.167 (+32%), downtown vivid-pixel share 3.3% -> 9.0%. The tile-coverage contract is untouched — Esri source, native z15, view z18 — so the blank-map fix cannot regress (nav-tile-coverage stays 5/5 unmodified). Satellite/hillshade layers (v240) carry their own classes and NO lift: aerial photos are already true colour. The v125 no-filter rule is superseded for this layer on this evidence (its hot-pink failure was OSM salmon motorways under a lift; Esri has no such band). REPRODUCTION-FIRST: new tools/nav-map-colors-v239-test.js — 5 RED on the shipped build (no street class, no lift rule), 9/9 GREEN after including a live drive-world run pinning class + coverage opts together. REGRESSIONS: navigator 178/180, drive-surface 31/31, nav-lanes 30/30, nav-lane-info 34/34, nav-inset 19/19, nav-popup 20/20, nav-cutoff 14/14, navigator-screen 39 + its 1 parked baseline failure (verified identical with this change stashed) — all at baseline. Standing pin move 238 -> 239. Native unchanged (v42 OTA pointer; no new APK). Machine-green is preparation — the verdict is his next real drive.",
